## Noncommercial Purpose

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.

Commercial purposes are not permitted. A commercial
purpose is any purpose principally aimed at generating
profit or enabling others to do so. The following purposes
are never commercial, even if the licensor could receive
payment for the purpose:

1. Providing software to others free of charge.
2. Contributing software to free or open source projects.
3. Providing research as part of the requirements of a
   degree program, or for publication in a peer-reviewed
   journal, or as part of academic research.

